**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `kit-acceptance`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitAcceptanceTests`
- `unit-tests`: `BerremanTests.BiaxialInverseTests`

**How to implement.** BiaxialInverseTests' measurement design moves into `BerremanTestSupport` beside its ground truth, so the Planner's acceptance facts (step 475) read the normal-incidence and full designs instead of transcribing them (the S14.1 brief 'For a normal-incidence-only BiaxialInverseTests design, it flags g12, g13 and g23 … Move a design definition into BerremanTestSupport if a fact needs it outside its class'; 001 §M; AGENTS.md 'Reuse, never copy'). This is a MOVE (.spec-md §4; .spec-md §7): after the step each moved name is declared once. (1) New `Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/BiaxialDesign.fs`, `module BerremanTestSupport.BiaxialDesign`, appended at the end of `BerremanTestSupport.fsproj`'s compile list (after `BiaxialSample.fs`, whose `referenceWaveLength` it reads) with no comment. It receives from `BiaxialInverseTests` (`BiaxialInverseTests.fs:plate` to `:fullConfigurations`), with the measurement-set banner (thickness, the three cuts and their transverse planes, the oblique sweeps) and their docs: `plate`, `configuration`, `principalCuts`, `b1`, `b2`, `b3` and `fullConfigurations`; and the ablation fact's local `normalOn` (in `the cuts buy the gyration DIAGONAL and only the tilt buys its OFF-DIAGONAL`) as `normalIncidenceOn (cut : SampleCut) : MeasurementConfiguration list`, its body unchanged (the four azimuths 0, 22.5, 45 and 67.5 degrees at normal incidence, transmitted) and a one-line doc. `configuration` reads `referenceWaveLength` (`BerremanTestSupport/BiaxialSample.fs`), the value the class's `waveLength` alias holds. `b1` becomes `principalCuts |> List.collect normalIncidenceOn`, the same twelve configurations in the same order (cut by cut, azimuth by azimuth), so the azimuth list is written once. It opens what they read (`MuellerInverse`, `OpticalConstructor.Optimization.MuellerFitting`, the engine's `Constants` and `Media`, `BerremanTestSupport.BiaxialSample`), reads no name of the `BerremanTests` namespace, and its module doc says in one to three lines that it is spec 0044's biaxial measurement design, shared by `BiaxialInverseTests` and the Planner's facts (spec 0050 S14.1). (2) `Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialInverseTests.fs` deletes those declarations and their banner and opens `BerremanTestSupport.BiaxialDesign` after its last `open`; its ablation fact deletes the local `normalOn` and builds `zOnly`, `zAndX` and `everyCutNormal` from `normalIncidenceOn`; `waveLength`, `forward`, `observe`, `perturbedStart`, `box`, `blindStart`, `wideBox`, the noisy helpers and every fact stay. `FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests` and the absorbing suites keep their own designs and do not open the module. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4): every configuration list holds the same configurations in the same order. No test is added or removed. `BiaxialInverseTests`, the class whose design moved, is selected (about 997 s).

**Acceptance.** After the move, `Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/BiaxialDesign.fs` MUST declare the biaxial plate, configuration, principal cuts, `normalIncidenceOn`, B1-B3 and the full set once, `b1` being `principalCuts |> List.collect normalIncidenceOn`, and `BiaxialInverseTests` MUST read them from it and declare none of them; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class `BerremanTests.BiaxialInverseTests`, its numbers and count unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s45 invariants MUST pass.
